{'symbol': 'TSLA', 'date': '2019-11-19 22:30:00', 'title': 'A CALIFORNIA FEDERAL JUDGE ORDERS DEFAMATION LAWSUIT AGAINST TESLA AND CEO', 'text': "A CALIFORNIA FEDERAL JUDGE HAS ORDERED A DEFAMATION LAWSUIT AGAINST TESLA AND CEO TO MOVE ON TO A JURY TRIAL. U.S. DISTRICT JUDGE STEPHEN WILSON ON TUESDAY DENIED MUSK'S REQUEST TO DISMISS THE CHARGES -- RULING THAT BRITISH EXPLORER AND CAVE DIVER VERSON UNSWORTH, WHO MUSK CRITICIZED, IS NOT A PUBLIC FIGURE. THE DECISION MEANS UNSWORTH'S SUIT WILL HAVE A LOWER BURDEN OF PROOF IN COURT WHEN THE TRIAL STARTS DEC. 3."}